00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:09.260 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  from the openings title splash screen  sonic manias presentation is  intoxicating it's colorful retro 2d  graphics and vibrant 90s inspired pop  soundtrack is enough to make any Sega  Genesis fans squeal and excitement but  Sonic's latest outing isn't only  concerned with reminding you of his  golden years Sonic mania exceeds  expectations what a new game in the  franchise can play and look like  managing to simultaneously be a charming  celebration of the past and a natural  progression of the series's classic 2d  formula  [Music]  sonic mania makes a strong first  impression thanks to amazing visuals and  music its presentation replicates the  charming aesthetic of Sonic's earliest  games with thorough detail the new  sprite animations add an extra layer of  personality to the iconic characters  that's a joy to see in motion the game  also sports an assortment of new music  tracks and remixes of greatest hits that  are incredibly catchy and well  orchestrated  [Music]  both visuals and music work together in  Sonic mania to build an aesthetic that's  evocative of earlier games but in a  pleasing style that feels contemporary  all on its own on top of Sonic manias  fantastic presentation the game also  controls like a classic style Sonic game  you have the option to play as sonic  tails or knuckles from the get-go the  movement physics and overall feel of  each character or distinct yet familiar  staying faithful to the originals the  gang's unique abilities remain intact  albeit with one exception Sonic has a  new drop - which allows him to quickly  roll forward after a jump it's a small  addition but it provides a handy new way  to pick up speed or avoid incoming  danger level design is that the series  is best here  sporting 12 zones that are each  meticulously designed with cleverly  placed obstacles and varied pathways  that keep you guessing and thanks to the  visibility granted by the widescreen  aspect ratio and the smooth frame rate  your awareness and sense of control  running through zone feels better than  Sonic's classic outings ever did it also  helps that levels are designed around  the abilities of each character while  Sonic can blaze a trail through a zone  knuckles and Tails can find other paths  beyond his reach thanks to the  respective climbing and flying abilities  which often lead to new ways of  experiencing the same stage and you're  rewarded for taking the time to play  them as on some occasions they even get  completely new zones to explore that are  designed specifically around their  abilities  [Music]  sonic mania closely follows in the  exhilarating sense of speed of its  forebears however it expands upon the  familiar with new ideas of its own this  is most apparent when you play remixed  versions of older zones from the first  five games for example sonic manias  version of Sonic 2 s chemical plant zone  introduces a mechanic where you  constantly jump on jelly to bounce  upwards to new parts of the level  changes like this liven up the design of  well-known levels offering fresh and  gratifying new experiences new zones  deliver plenty of inventive concepts  that diversify and build upon the  series's fast-paced level design whether  it's by encouraging you to freeze  yourself into an ice block to smash  through walls or challenging you to  figure out a maze-like sequence of gates  to reach the end of a zone the ideas the  game explorers give it a strong sense of  identity compared to the originals every  level culminates in a boss fight ranging  from relatively simple to demanding  set-piece battles where you go  head-to-head with Eggman and his minions  one has you dodging projectiles as you  use a series of poles to propel yourself  towards a spider robot  [Music]  phosphites offer great balance of  difficulty steadily challenging and  entertaining you in numerous ways as you  progress the more you play Sonic mania  the more it rewards you with reasons to  keep playing but one of the most  compelling reasons to plays owns comes  from Secrets sonic manias term for  unlocks that give you access to new  characters and abilities for example you  can play through the entire campaign  using the Sonic 3 into the shield  ability however the caveat is that you  can only turn on secrets when playing  without save functionality so if you  want to use these abilities you can only  do so by going through the game in one  sitting  it's a strange limitation that restricts  your ability to take advantage of  everything the game has to offer  [Music]  for years the Sonic series has chased  the legacy of its early games repeatedly  delivering experiences that either came  close or failed to recapture the spirit  that made them classics sonic mania  methodically uses its sentimental appeal  to great effect but in the process it  heals the wounds inflicted by its most  disappointing predecessors and surpasses  the series is best with its smart and  interpretive design an excellent 2d  platformer Sonic mania goes beyond  expectations managing to not only be a  proper evolution of the series's iconic  formula but the best Sonic game ever  made  [Music]

